## Context
The route skill defines "doors" only as providers. Nothing says how a worker
is reached in each runtime. Launch doors are two: a subagent inside the
current CLI (Claude Code, Pi, Codex), and a headless CLI started from bash
with a given model (`claude -p`, `pi --print`, `codex exec`, `vibe -p`).
Recipes are scattered (`skills/hunt`, `skills/review-pr:151-186`,
`docs/trace-ab-2026-06.md:105`, `skills/coaching/seat-runner.sh`).

## Scope
- `skills/route/routes.json`: launch doors by runtime (Claude Code, Pi,
  Codex, Vibe): subagent form (what to pin) and headless command template
  with a model flag; note the Vibe limit (file tools denied headless, ticket 1017).
- Rewrite `skills/route/SKILL.md`: the orchestrator chooses from the grid
  using general recommendations; replace the two-stage cluster-then-script
  decision. Add one pointer line per runtime ("If you are Codex, read
  `routes-recommendations-codex.md`") and the four recommendation files.
- Model names may appear in the recommendation files and route data. Amend
  `test_portable_skill_instructions_do_not_name_models` with an exemption for
  `skills/route/` in this PR.
- Amend the non-goals in `docs/portable-model-capability-policy.md:417-421`
  (the harness now holds a grid; `grid.json` already contradicted them).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Each launch-door template run once, evidence in the log
- [ ] `model: haiku` resolves to Haiku 5.5 in a live session
- [ ] Four per-runtime recommendation files and their pointer lines exist
- [ ] The no-model-names test passes with the `skills/route/` exemption
- [ ] `make check` passes
